  "query_preview": "..(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 310 PM EDT SAT SEP 5 2026\n\nLooking ahead towards the beginning of next week, upper level\nridging will begin to build over the central CONUS as the\naforementioned upper level high pushes east towards the\nMississippi Valley. As a result, dry conditions should prevail,\nwith highs mostly in the mid to upper 80s through much of next\nweek. Towards the end of the week however, the upper ridge will\nbegin to flatten out as an upper level shortwave trough pushes\nthrough the Upper Mississippi Valley/Great Lakes regions, bringing\nthe next chance for precipitation.",
